      "evidence": "template/scripts/dev.py: `[\"git\", \"rev-parse\", \"--path-format=absolute\", \"--git-path\", \"info/exclude\"]` with `check=True`. This ships to downstream projects. The change adds no version guard, and no fallback that resolves a relative result against `root`. The code it replaces did resolve a relative path against `root`.",
      "id": "git-path-format-absolute-version",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "The exclude writer now depends on `git rev-parse --path-format=absolute`, which needs Git 2.31 or newer. On older Git, `ensure_local_generated_excludes` raises CalledProcessError because of `check=True`. The previous `--git-dir` call worked on any Git version."
    }
